
============================================================================
1. the U_t threshold is alpha, not 1 - delta  [MY LAST PASS WAS WRONG]
============================================================================
  U_t = # t-block starts in W_{5t}.  On a surviving orbit every
  boundary realizes infinitely many blocks, hence at least t, so
  EVERY VISIT to W_{5t} is itself a t-block start, and the visits
  are distinct because x -> (81x+c)/64 is strictly increasing on
  positive states.  So U_t is at least the visit count.
  The visit count is 3 on a set of scales of density 1 - delta and
  2 on density delta, so
    liminf (1/T) sum U_t >= 3 - delta = alpha = 2.9424745962.
  An upper average of 2 along an unbounded sequence of T therefore
  contradicts survival.  The reference average of U_t is 1.

  RETRACTION.  Yesterday I wrote that the unrestricted count is
  closed because E[U_t] = 1 exceeds the threshold 0.9424746 by 6%.
  That compared the wrong pair.  The 0.9424746 threshold belongs to
  C_t (three-visit starts, one per scale); the unrestricted count
  must be weighed against the visits WITH MULTIPLICITY, which is
  alpha = 2.9424746.  The margin is therefore not -6% but
    2.000000 / 1.000000 = a factor 2 of slack to the usable
    threshold, and 2.942475 to the forced value.
  So the unrestricted window count is NOT closed.  My claim that a
  proof must use the bottom 24.86%% of each window is withdrawn.

============================================================================
2. the B_t <= 14t target: the chain is valid
============================================================================
  (a) GROWTH.  With Y = 17x + 73 the two blocks give exactly
        64 Y' = 81 Y        (B),
        64 Y' = 81 Y - 136  (A),
      so Y_{j+1} <= rho Y_j with equality iff the block is B.
      checked on 6 admissible states, both labels.  Hence
        Y_b <= rho^b Y_0, i.e. 17x_0 + 73 >= (17x_b + 73) rho^-b.
  (b) PIGEONHOLE.  A seed completing t+b blocks has boundaries
      x_0 < x_1 < ... < x_b, and x_j realizes t+b-j >= t blocks, so
      all b+1 are distinct t-block starts.  If x_b < H_t all b+1
      would lie below H_t, but only b = B_t do.  So x_b >= H_t and
        17 r_min(t+b) + 73 >= (17 H_t + 73) (64/81)^b.
      worked instance, b = B_48 = 1: any seed completing 49 blocks
      has x_1 >= 2^241, hence x_0 >= 2.792055e+72.
      This is weaker than the direct depth-48 count (which gives
      r_min(49) >= 2^241 = 3.534e+72) -- the framework is asymptotic,
      not a sharpening at any fixed depth.
  (c) THE EXPONENT.  The bound grows iff 2^{5t} rho^-b -> infinity,
      i.e. iff b <= 5 log_rho 2 - o(1) times t, and
        5 alpha = log_rho 32 = 14.712372981.
      verified by integer comparison: 3^56 < 2^89 < 2^95 < 3^60, so
      14 < log_rho 32 < 15 and the choice 14 is safe.
      With b = 14t the lower bound is 2 (32/rho^14)^t with
        32/rho^14 = 2^89/3^56 = 1.182713,
      so r_min(t + B_t) >= 2 * 1.1827^t -> infinity.
        t = 100   : r_min(t+B_t) >= 10^7.6
        t = 1000  : r_min(t+B_t) >= 10^73.2
  (d) Monotonicity of r_min (Theorem M) upgrades a subsequence to
      the full limit, so B_t <= 14t at arbitrarily large t gives
      r_min(q) -> infinity.  CHAIN VALID.

