============================================================================
4. B_t <= 14t infinitely often follows from ANY finite average
============================================================================
  If B_t > 14t for every t >= t_0 then
    sum_{t<=T} B_t > 14 * (T^2 - t_0^2)/2 ~ 7 T^2,
  so (1/T) sum_{t<=T} B_t -> infinity.  Contrapositive:
    liminf_T (1/T) sum_{t<=T} B_t < infinity
  implies B_t <= 14t at arbitrarily large t, hence r_min(q) -> inf.
  So the usable target is weaker than an average of 2 for U_t: ANY
  constant bound on the average of B_t along one unbounded
  sequence of T suffices, because the linear allowance 14t does
  the rest.  That is the weakest sufficient condition the
  programme has produced.

