6. verdict
============================================================================
  CORRECTED.  My last pass closed the unrestricted-count route on a
  mis-paired comparison.  Weighed against the visit count with
  multiplicity, the threshold is alpha = 2.9424746 and the usable
  target is an average of 2 -- a factor 2 above the reference
  value 1, not 6%% below a threshold.  The route is open.
  CONFIRMED.  The B_t <= 14t chain: growth 64Y' <= 81Y with
  Y = 17x+73, the b+1 distinct starts, x_b >= H_t, the exponent
  5 log_rho 2 = 14.712373 > 14 (integer-certified by 3^56 < 2^89),
  and monotonicity. B_t <= 14t at arbitrarily large t does settle
  the restricted claim.
  CONFIRMED by census.  B_t <= 14t at every t = 3..40 and at 48;
  max B_t = 6 against an allowance of 14t >= 42; observed average
  1.711 against the reference 2.
  NEW, UNCONDITIONAL.  B_t <= 2^{ceil((5t-2)/6)}: a start below
  H_t is determined by its first ~5t/6 letters, because
  v_2(s_i) = 3+6i.  This is a factor 2^{t/6} below the trivial
  2^t, it is the ceiling of the 2-adic argument, and it is still
  exponential.
  THE GAP, in its weakest form yet.  Any constant bound on
  liminf (1/T) sum_{t<=T} B_t.  No paired zeros, no bottom-24.86%%
  resolution, no single-scale bound, and a factor ~7t of slack at
  each scale.  What is still missing is the same thing as always:
  an equidistribution estimate for the residues r_w in a short
  interval -- but now needed only on average and only to within
  a linearly growing factor.
  SCOPE.  Restricted two-block positive-integer claim only.

